Z||000000||bandit1||08-02-99||03:29 PM||||Is it true that you have to pull the engine from underneath???  
Z||000001||SCCA FIERO||08-02-99||05:34 PM||||It can be pulled from the top, but I have not done it that way. It is not as bad as it sounds(from underneath). I have done it 3 times and the last time it took about 2 hours to have the cradle on the ground. 
Z||000002||Shaun41178||08-02-99||11:02 PM||||I have pulled the engine from the top and found it to be very easy to do.  I have never taken the Fiero engine out through the bottom so I can not comment on which way is easier/better.<p>One thing that I like about the engine coming out through the top is that the tranny is still in the car and can be moved around if needed.  If the cradle is dropped the the car becomes immobile until the cradle gets put back in.  I needed to move my car around several times while so it worked out quite well.<p>I did a write up on what it takes to remove the engine from the top if you are interested.  go to  http://members.aol.com/shaun41178 and scroll down and you can't miss it.
